# The catch-up infers that a marker predates the re-created incarnation from its
# generation or initialised flag, instead of reading the incarnation the marker
# carries (#5716). A duplicate activation of the shard root re-seeding
# concurrently runs the catch-up after the first activation has seeded the marker
# at the floor plus one and run the init fence. It reads that live marker, raises
# the shard root's floor to its generation and resets it, while the first
# activation keeps stamping its cached generation, now at the floor: the WAL
# refuses its claims, and #5705's guard fails a live tree's writes as deleted.
# Moved from the design's LiveGenerationAboveFloorCatchUpRetiresLiveMarker.
MODULE: LiveGenerationAboveFloorCatchUpRetiresLiveMarker
TARGET: LiveGenerationAboveFloor
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the re-seed catch-up retires a marker the re-created incarnation seeded
PERTURBS: CatchUp

--- FIND
    /\ caught' = TRUE
    /\ ~markNew
--- REPLACE
    /\ caught' = TRUE
\* MUTATION: the marker's incarnation is not checked.
--- END
